You have a .NET app named App1.  

You need to upload App1 to GitHub Packages.  

How should you complete the command?

<Dropdown
  blanks={[{"id":"command","options":["dotnet","git","make","npm"],"answer":"dotnet"},{"id":"operation","options":["nuget add source","nuget push","pack","publish"],"answer":"nuget push"}]}
  template={"{{command}} {{operation}} \"bin/Release/app1.1.0.0.nupkg\" --api-key PAT_TOKEN --source \"github\""}
  templateMode={"code"}
  explanation={"`dotnet nuget push` publishes an existing NuGet `.nupkg` package to the configured source. The command supports both `--api-key` for the GitHub personal access token and `--source` for the package source.\
\
